# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Applies to every subproject, present and future
#
# This repository holds four separate apps (studio, beatsunlimited-app,
# noizes-gallery-android, noizes-gallery-pwa). Until now the ignore file named
# none of them: three arrived after it was written, and each brought its own
# dependency and output directories with no coverage.
#
# The cost of that gap: a plain `git add` on a newly dropped-in subproject
# staged 980 files and 95 MB of Gradle output — a debug APK, merged dex, file
# hash caches. It was caught by hand and never pushed, but only because
# someone happened to look.
#
# These patterns are deliberately unanchored, so a fifth app added tomorrow is
# covered before anyone thinks about it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Dependencies
**/node_modules/

# Build output
**/dist/
**/out/
**/target/
**/.next/
**/.svelte-kit/
**/.turbo/

# NOTE: `build/` is deliberately NOT ignored globally. It is an output
# directory in most projects but a source directory in others —
# noizes-gallery-pwa/build/ holds sites-vite-plugin.ts, which its vite.config
# imports at line 4. A blanket rule would silently delete a file the build
# depends on from the index. Ignore build/ per project, below, where it really
# is output.

# Tooling and machine-local state
**/.gradle/
**/.kotlin/
**/.wrangler/
**/.vinext/
**/coverage/
**/.DS_Store
**/local.properties
.netlify
.gstack/

# Secrets. Never commit a real .env; the .example files are the contract.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project-specific
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Reproducible immersive-reference-album outputs and preserved source
# downloads. Run `npm run build` in that directory to recreate build/ and dist/.
examples/immersive-reference-album/build/
examples/immersive-reference-album/sources/original/
examples/immersive-reference-album/screenshots/*.png
!examples/immersive-reference-album/screenshots/09-integrated-viewer-mobile.png

# Transcendence edition: analysis and textures are computed from the source
# recording by scripts/analyze-transcendence.mjs and
# scripts/generate-textures-transcendence.mjs. Regenerate rather than commit.
examples/immersive-reference-album/transcendence/analysis/
examples/immersive-reference-album/transcendence/assets/
examples/immersive-reference-album/screenshots/transcendence-review/

# Android gallery app: Gradle and KSP output. Here build/ genuinely is output —
# ~95 MB of dex, APKs and hash caches. Rebuild with ./gradlew.
noizes-gallery-android/build/
noizes-gallery-android/app/build/
